                                <br>She has completed her MBBS from K.J. Somaiya Medical College, followed by her Post graduate studies from Seth G.S. Medical College & K.E.M. Hospital, Mumbai. She has undergone specialized laparoscopic training under Dr. Hafeez Rehman at Sunrise Hospital, Kochi, and has worked in the Department of Oncology- Gynaecology at Tata Memorial Hospital. 
                                Dr. Jain is a life member of FOGSI, IAGE, and the Jain Doctors Federation and has received many awards and recognition for her outstanding performance and contribution to the field.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="best-doctor-outer">
                        <div class="image">
                            <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/daoju0r3c/image/upload/v1755411772/WhatsApp_Image_2025-07-24_at_15.20.54_2_1_pc2p4r.png" class="img-fluid" alt="best-doctors" />
                            <a href="#" class="link"></a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="content-inner">
                            <h2> Dr. Jignesh Mepani</a></h2>
                            <span>Bachelor of Physiotherapy | <br> Certified Mulligan <br> Practitioner </span>
                            <p>With over 18 years of experience, I specialize in helping individuals restore movement, manage pain, and regain function. I'm a Certified Mulligan Practitioner, trained in gentle, pain-free manual therapy techniques that support effective recovery. 
                                <br>My 8-year tenure at Breach Candy Hospital across ICUs, wards, and OPDs shaped my patient-focused, result-driven approach. I'm committed to providing precise care that helps you move better, heal faster, and live pain-free.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="best-doctor-outer">
                        <div class="image">
                            <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/daoju0r3c/image/upload/v1755412004/image_7_tmlmzy.png" class="img-fluid" alt="best-doctors" />
                            <a href="#" class="link"></a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="content-inner">
                            <h2> Dr. Pulkit Popat</a></h2>
                            <span>Occupational Therapist | Neuro & Musculoskeletal Rehabilitation <br> Specialist</span>
                            <p>I'm a licensed Occupational Therapist with a degree from Seth G.S. Medical College & KEM Hospital, Mumbai, and over four years of experience in neuro and musculoskeletal rehabilitation. I specialize in stroke recovery, spinal cord injuries, orthopedic conditions, and chronic pain.
                                <br>With a patient-focused, evidence-based approach, I design personalized rehab plans that restore independence, improve function, and enhance quality of life.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="best-doctor-outer">
                        <div class="image">
                            <img src="" class="img-fluid" alt="doctors" />
                            <a href="#" class="link"></a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="content-inner">
                            <h2> Dr. Harshita Saraogi</a></h2>
                            <span>Bachelor of Physiotherapy | <br> Certified Mulligan <br> Practitioner </span>
                            <p>With over 18 years of experience, I specialize in helping individuals restore movement, manage pain, and regain function. I'm a Certified Mulligan Practitioner, trained in gentle, pain-free manual therapy techniques that support effective recovery. 
                                <br>My 8-year tenure at Breach Candy Hospital across ICUs, wards, and OPDs shaped my patient-focused, result-driven approach. I'm committed to providing precise care that helps you move better, heal faster, and live pain-free.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


